### Search contacts [GET /contacts/search?{email}&{mobile}]

Performs contacts search among permitted for the API enabled offices.

Accepted parameters: `email`, `mobile`.

More than one parameter can be passed to the API endpoint. Search will be performed using **OR** logic.

+ Request

    + Headers

            Authorization: Api-Key token=b3c7623c3ad30d34fec6226f90914b0af125dc06

+ Parameters

    + email (optional, string, `john@example.com`)

    + mobile (optional, string, `0400123456`)

+ Response 200 (application/json)

    + Body
    
            {
                "data": [
                    {
                        "id": 1,
                        "first_name": "John",
                        "last_name": "Smith",
                        "mobile": "0400123456",
                        "email": "john@example.com"
                    }
                ]
            }

### Create a contact [POST]

Creates a contact with provided in request body details (see Contact Attributes for the list of supported attributes).

Parameter `consultant_id` used to assign a Consultant - creator of a new contact.

+ Request (application/json)

    + Headers

            Authorization: Api-Key token=b3c7623c3ad30d34fec6226f90914b0af125dc06

    + Body
    
            {
                "contact": {
                    "first_name": "John",
                    "last_name": "Smith",
                    "mobile": "0404111222",
                    "email": "john.smith@example.com",
                    "consultant_id": 2
                }
            }

+ Response 201 (application/json)

        {
            "id": 1
        }

